---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const sections = [
  ['Install', 'Get the toolchain and build your first program.', '/docs/install'],
  ['The Tour', 'Learn by doing, in the browser — hello-locus to a distributed fleet.', '/tour'],
  ['The Book', 'The long-form guide: loci, memory, failure, the bus, placement.', '/docs/book'],
  ['Hale by Example', 'Annotated, copy-paste recipes for common tasks.', '/docs/examples'],
  ['Language spec', 'The authoritative reference — semantics, types, grammar.', '/docs/spec'],
  ['Standard library', 'The always-loaded std:: surface.', '/docs/stdlib'],
  ['CLI reference', 'build · check · run · test · fetch · fmt.', '/docs/cli'],
  ['Design rationale', 'The locked commitments and what was rejected.', '/docs/rationale'],
  ['Verification', 'Every static check the compiler runs, with severities.', '/docs/verification'],
];
---
<Base title="Hale documentation">
  <section class="container">
    <span class="tag">/docs</span>
    <h1>Documentation</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width:60ch;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      Hale already has an exhaustive specification. These pages present it — most
      content is drawn straight from the language spec.
    </p>
    <div class="grid cols-3">
      {sections.map(([h, p, href]) => (
        <a class="card" href={href} style="text-decoration:none;display:block;">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">{h}</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.95rem;">{p}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:2rem;">
      Most reference pages are placeholders in this early build; the spec source is
      complete and will be wired in next.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
